sxml transform - Transform a document with an XSLT 4.0 stylesheet

Usage: sxml transform [--initial-mode=NAME] [--initial-template=NAME] [--method=METHOD] [--param=NAME=VALUE]... [--result-directory=DIR] [--collection=DIR] [--code-language=LIBRARY]... [--output=FILE] [--force] STYLESHEET [INPUT]

Compiles the XSLT 4.0 stylesheet STYLESHEET and runs it.

With INPUT, the document becomes the global context item. Templates
are applied to it in the default mode, or in the mode that
--initial-mode names; or the template that --initial-template names is
called with INPUT as the context item. Without INPUT, the template
that --initial-template names, else xsl:initial-template, is called
without a context item.

When templates are applied to an INPUT file in a mode declared
streamable="yes" whose template rules are all guaranteed-streamable,
INPUT is streamed and is not the global context item.

The principal result goes to standard output, or to the file that
--output names, serialized as the stylesheet's xsl:output says;
--method replaces the method. xsl:message output goes to standard
error. --param=NAME=VALUE binds the stylesheet parameter $NAME to
xs:untypedAtomic(VALUE). Included and imported modules and documents
are read from local files.

Result documents with an href are written only with
--result-directory=DIR: DIR, which must exist, is the base output
URI, so an href resolves against it, and a result document whose URI
is not a file below DIR is an error. Directories below DIR are made
as needed. Without the option each is reported on standard error
and not written.

Files are written only when the transformation succeeds; one that
exists is replaced only with --force.

An error is reported on standard error as
  STYLESHEET:LINE:COLUMN: err:CODE: description

Exit status: 0 on success, 1 for an error in the stylesheet or a
document that is not well-formed, 3 when a file cannot be read or
written.

Options:
  -h, --help                   Show this help and exit
      --initial-mode=NAME      Mode whose template rules process INPUT, instead of the default mode
      --initial-template=NAME  Named template to call, instead of applying templates to INPUT
      --method=METHOD          Serialization method of the result, replacing the stylesheet's (one of: adaptive, xml, xhtml, html, text, json, csv)
      --param=NAME=VALUE       Bind stylesheet parameter $NAME to xs:untypedAtomic(VALUE) (repeatable)
      --result-directory=DIR   Write result documents with an href into the existing directory DIR
      --collection=DIR         Directory whose XML files are the default collection
      --code-language=LIBRARY  Load a tree-sitter language for tree-sitter:parse from a shared library (repeatable)
  -o, --output=FILE            Write the result to FILE instead of standard output
      --force                  Replace files that exist instead of refusing

Arguments:
  STYLESHEET  File holding the principal stylesheet module
  INPUT       XML document to transform, the global context item; - reads standard input

Examples:
  sxml transform outline.xsl draft.xml
  sxml transform --param='heading=Latch requirements' outline.xsl draft.xml
  sxml transform hello.xsl
  sxml transform --method=xml outline.xsl - < draft.xml
  sxml transform --result-directory=site --output=site/index.html pages.xsl draft.xml
